# =============================================================================
# GradPrep AI — Environment Variables
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values for your Supabase project.
# NEVER commit the real .env file — it is listed in .gitignore.
#
# Where to get each value:
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL             → Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API → Project URL
#   VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID      → Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → General → Reference ID
#   VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY → Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API → anon / public key
# =============================================================================

# VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://<project-ref>.supabase.co"
# VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="<project-ref>"
# VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="<anon-key>"

# =============================================================================
# PIPER VOICE SERVICE (local / self-hosted TTS — replaces ElevenLabs)
# =============================================================================
# Start the Python voice service first:
#   cd voice-service && python main.py
# Then set the URL so the Edge Function (voice-tts) can proxy to it.
# Leave empty to fall back to the browser Web Speech API.
#
# VITE_VOICE_SERVICE_URL="http://localhost:8001"   ← direct local Piper service
# Leave unset in production; the Supabase Edge Function proxies Piper there.
#
# SERVER-SIDE SECRETS — set in Supabase Edge Function Secrets:
# Supabase Dashboard → Project → Edge Functions → Secrets
#   PIPER_SERVICE_URL="http://your-server:8001"    ← URL of the Piper service
#   PIPER_API_KEY=""                               ← match API_SECRET_KEY in voice-service/.env

# =============================================================================
# SERVER-SIDE SECRETS — set these in Supabase Edge Function Secrets only.
# NEVER prefix with VITE_ — that would expose them to the browser.
# =============================================================================

# --- Google Gemini (AI interview questions, answer evaluation, LUSY chat) ---
# GEMINI_API_KEY="AIza...."       ← already configured

# --- OpenAI Whisper STT (accurate interview answer transcription) ---
# OPENAI_API_KEY="sk-..."         ← required for Whisper transcription

# --- Admin ---
# ADMIN_EMAILS="you@example.com"  ← already configured

# --- Razorpay Checkout (set in Supabase Edge Function Secrets only) ---
# Keep the key ID and secret from the same Razorpay environment (test or live).
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID="rzp_test_..."
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET="..."
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET="..."

# =============================================================================
# REMOVED (ElevenLabs — replaced by Piper TTS)
# =============================================================================
# The following secrets are no longer used and can be safely removed from
# Supabase Edge Function Secrets after verifying the Piper service works:
#
#   ELEVENLABS_API_KEY
#   ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID_FEMALE
#   ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID_MALE
#   ELEVENLABS_MODEL_ID
#
# Do NOT remove them from external ElevenLabs account dashboards until you
# have confirmed the Piper service is stable in your environment.
